// Showcase of all three regex operations a provider script can call
// (regex_is_match / regex_find / regex_count), each surfaced as a field of
// the `Regex::Analyze` provider's output and projected in the policy.
//
// UNWRAPPED form on purpose — no `guardrails { … }` block. The provider
// calls sit directly in an ordinary Cedar `when { … }`, recognized because
// `Regex::Analyze` is a declared provider; the projections and comparisons
// are plain Cedar, combined with `&&`.
//
// Permit `Read` only when the document:
//   1. starts with an uppercase letter        (is_match of `^[A-Z]`),
//   2. contains at least three digit chars     (count of `[0-9]` >= 3), and
//   3. its first run of digits is exactly "42" (first_match of `[0-9]+`).

permit (
    principal,
    action == Drupe::Action::"Read",
    resource
)
when {
    Regex::Analyze(context.input.document, "^[A-Z]").is_match == true
    && Regex::Analyze(context.input.document, "[0-9]").count >= 3
    && Regex::Analyze(context.input.document, "[0-9]+").first_match == "42"
};
